1. Tiny Receipt Reader Digit Slots 2M
   Source: https://huggingface.co/ivere27/tiny-receipt-reader-digit-slots-2m
   Revision: c9fa07886f99334ea820bfe312d6b4771d9460b0
   License: Apache-2.0; model/LICENSE.txt in the digit package, downloaded from
   the pinned public source release.
   Changes: FP32 ONNX conversion through VolvoxAI. The default
   conv4-linear2 profile uses joint weight QAT, INT4 convolution weights and
   INT2/group32 dense weights, followed by static INT8 convolution calibration.
   Packed dense layers use dynamic INT8 arithmetic; other selected operations
   remain FP32. The optional W8A8 build calibrates INT8 convolutions. Exact
   graph/weight hashes and fitting algorithms are recorded in build-info.json
   and model/manifest.json in each corresponding browser package. Default builds
   download the public FP32 source, train and calibrate with synthetic receipts
   000000 through 000223, and reserve 000224 through 000255 for validation.
   Weight training uses CPU by default, with CUDA available through QAT_BACKEND;
   convolution calibration uses CPU. Historical evaluated artifact identities
   and scope remain in digit/frozen-profiles.json and benchmarks/ in source for
   optional explicit imports. Fresh builds can produce different weights.

2. Tiny unaveraged VQA Structured QA 21M
   Source: https://huggingface.co/ivere27/tiny-receipt-vqa-structured-qa-21m
   Revision: f536c6ed181ca88929214f0bbc08f126f148c7ae
   License: Apache-2.0; original model/LICENSE.txt and model/NOTICE.txt in VQA ZIP,
   downloaded from the pinned public source release.
   Changes: FP32 encoder/decoder conversion through VolvoxAI; masked question
   padding to 192, batch 1, int32 IDs/masks, positive-length masked KV sentinel,
   SiLU numerical migration and common subexpression elimination. The default
   W4A8 PTQ profile packs 67 dense layers at INT4/group32 with dynamic INT8
   activations; 13 convolutions use static INT8. Identical constants and token
   embeddings share storage. Other selected operations remain FP32. Default builds
   download the public FP32 source and perform PTQ with all 256 bundled synthetic
   receipts. Generated graphs, weight shards and manifests are stored in local
   caches before packaging. Historical evaluated artifact identities remain in
   vqa/frozen-profiles.json for optional explicit imports; fresh builds can differ.

Model provenance and modifications are recorded in each package's build-info.json
and model/manifest.json. Private calibration/evaluation images and questions are
not redistributed with the public source or either browser package. The public
documentation includes two unchanged synthetic Korean receipt examples from the
pinned model repositories, together with selected public example questions and
expected answers. These are not captured user receipts. Their original URLs,
revisions and SHA256 hashes are listed in docs/assets/examples/sources.json.
The Apache-2.0 license is in the root LICENSE. The original VQA notice is
retained below. Documentation examples are not added to the
extension packages.

The public source also includes synth/: 256 original
synthetic receipt PNGs and their generated content/glyph-coordinate annotations,
distributed under this repository's Apache-2.0 license. Their image pixels are
procedurally rendered; store names, address prefixes and item names come from a
text bank built from existing receipt annotations. Captured receipt images and
their original annotation files are not included. Generation uses rendered Noto
Sans CJK and DejaVu glyphs; no font binaries are distributed in this dataset.
The dataset manifest records image/annotation hashes and generation provenance.
Calibration data is included in source exports and excluded from extension packages.

